WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.436
Ten dollar a day childcare.

00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:04.875
The promise versus the waitlists.

00:00:04.875 --> 00:00:12.579
The federal government committed thirty billion dollars over five years to reduce childcare fees to ten dollars per day by 2026.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:14.455
Fees came down.

00:00:14.455 --> 00:00:16.545
But waitlists exploded.

00:00:16.545 --> 00:00:20.227
New spaces were not created as fast as demand grew.

00:00:20.227 --> 00:00:25.840
Early childhood educators cannot afford to work in childcare at the subsidized wage rates.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.659
The paradox: cheaper childcare that families can't access because there aren't enough spaces or workers.

00:00:31.659 --> 00:00:33.181
The promise.

00:00:33.181 --> 00:00:36.113
Thirty billion dollars over five years.

00:00:36.113 --> 00:00:39.852
Bilateral agreements with all provinces and territories.

00:00:39.852 --> 00:00:44.477
Reduce average fees to ten dollars per day by March 2026.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:48.852
Create two hundred and fifty thousand new regulated childcare spaces.

00:00:48.852 --> 00:00:53.795
The promise was modeled on Quebec's system — which took twenty years to fully build out.

00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:56.227
The subsidy paradox pattern.

00:00:56.227 --> 00:00:59.318
Subsidize the price without building the supply.

00:00:59.318 --> 00:01:00.921
Fees drop.

00:01:00.921 --> 00:01:02.727
Demand surges.

00:01:02.727 --> 00:01:04.738
Waitlists explode.

00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:07.647
Workers leave because wages don't keep up.

00:01:07.647 --> 00:01:10.863
Announce the fee reduction as a historic achievement.

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:14.488
Blame provinces for not creating spaces fast enough.

00:01:14.488 --> 00:01:21.840
The same pattern as healthcare: universal access promised, but the system doesn't have enough doctors, nurses, or beds to deliver.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.784
The promise is real.

00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:26.534
The delivery infrastructure is not.
